From 4dbe5d69660c925890e5516037e4c8ebc38c82b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:00:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(api_server): session-stream disconnect during worker
 teardown no longer discards the reply

The disconnect drain for POST /api/sessions/{id}/chat/stream decided "never
started -> cancel" from `_active_run_agents` alone. `_run_agent`'s worker
unregisters the agent in its `finally`, before the loop sees the result, so a
client disconnect landing in that window cancelled a turn that had already
finished: the run read "cancelled" with no output and the handler raised
CancelledError (api_server.py:3790). That is the CI flake of
test_session_stream_records_reply_text_for_post_disconnect_recovery (run
41592552337): its test thread releases the agent right after run_started, so on
a throttled runner the worker could finish before the handler wrote the
disconnecting frame.

The route now passes `agent_ref` to `_run_agent` (set once the agent is built,
never cleared) and the drain only cancels when no agent was ever built;
otherwise it interrupts and awaits the turn. The drain moved to the new
sibling `api_server_session_stream.py` (keeps the facade under its ratchet).

Regression test holds the worker inside its teardown (after the unregister) and
disconnects there; red on main with the exact CI CancelledError, green here.
